<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  MasterClock — pt (European Portuguese)

  This file is the European variant. Brazilian devices resolve values-pt-rBR first and fall back
  here string by string, so that file only carries the words that actually differ — "tela" for
  "ecrã", "configurações" for "definições", "compartilhar" for "partilhar", and the -ônico
  spellings. Everything else is shared and lives here.

  Mode names (Fischer, Byoyomi, Sudden Death…) and chess variant names are Kotlin literals rather
  than resources, so they stay in English by construction.

  app_name and settings_app_version are left out on purpose: they are the product name.

  Translated without a native reviewer, like the Spanish, German and Italian.
-->
